# Angular CLI Rules

When creating a new Angular component, ALWAYS use Angular CLI.

Use:

ng generate component <path>

or the short form:

ng g c <path>

NEVER manually create component files such as:
- .component.ts
- .component.html
- .component.scss
- .component.css
- .component.spec.ts

Do not create Angular component files manually when the component can be generated using Angular CLI.

For example, if asked to create:

src/app/shared/components/user-card

run:

ng g c shared/components/user-card

After generating the component, modify the generated files if necessary.

Always prefer Angular CLI for:
- Components
- Services
- Directives
- Pipes
- Guards
- Interceptors
- Interfaces/models when Angular CLI supports the requested artifact

For components, preserve the project's existing Angular CLI configuration and naming conventions.

