==================================================
PRODUCT COLLECTION
==================================================

The products collection represents the store products.

A product can contain fields such as:

- name
- brand
- categoryId
- gender
- price
- discount
- description
- imageUrl
- stock
- frameColor
- frameMaterial
- lensType
- isActive
- createdAt
- updatedAt

Use the Firestore document ID as the product identifier.

Do NOT create an additional "id" field unless there is a specific requirement.

Use Firestore Timestamp for:

- createdAt
- updatedAt

New Arrivals should NOT be a separate collection.

New Arrivals should be calculated using createdAt.

Example:

Products created within the last 30 days can be displayed as New Arrivals.

==================================================
CATEGORY COLLECTION
==================================================

The categories collection stores product categories.

Each product should reference a category using:

categoryId

Do not duplicate the entire category object inside products.

Example:

products
    categoryId: "sunglasses"

categories
    documentId: "sunglasses"

Category documents may contain:

- name
- imageUrl
- isActive
- createdAt
- updatedAt

