==================================================
ANGULAR ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

Use Angular 20 standalone components.

DO NOT use NgModules.

DO NOT use ng-content or content projection.

Compose UIs by importing standalone components and passing data with input() / output() / model().

Use lazy loading where appropriate.

Prefer:

loadComponent

for standalone route components.

Keep Firebase logic inside core services.

Do NOT put Firestore or Auth SDK calls directly inside components, stores, or templates.

Page components must inject the feature facade only.

Never inject the feature store or a Firestore service into a page component.

==================================================
FEATURE LAYER (MODELS / STORE / FACADE)
==================================================

Every domain feature that owns state must contain:

- models/
- store/
- facade/
- pages/ (and optional components/)

Layering:

Component
    ↓
Facade
    ↓
Store (state) + Data service (I/O)
    ↓
Firestore / Firebase Auth / localStorage

Store:

- Use Angular signal() for writable source state.
- Use computed() for derived values (filtered lists, totals, itemCount, canSubmit, isEmpty).
- Do not store derived values in a writable signal.
- Mutations stay private. The facade calls them.

Facade:

- Public API for the feature.
- Re-exposes readonly signals and computeds.
- Exposes commands (load, submit, addToCart, save).
- Orchestrates store + core services.

Models:

- Feature-specific types live in the feature models/ folder.
- Shared Firestore entities (Product, Category) live in core/models.

Layouts do not get a store or facade.

Home may compose other facades instead of owning product state.

Do not add NgRx or @ngrx/signals unless explicitly requested.

==================================================
STANDALONE AND REUSABLE COMPONENTS
==================================================

All components are standalone.

Reusable presentational components belong in:

shared/ui/

Examples:

- Button
- Text field
- Empty state
- Confirm dialog

Reusable components:

- Accept data through input() / model()
- Emit events through output()
- Do NOT use ng-content
- Do NOT talk to Firebase, stores, or facades

Feature-specific UI stays inside that feature's components/ folder.

==================================================
COMPONENT GENERATION
==================================================

NEVER create Angular components by writing files manually.

Always generate components with the Angular CLI:

ng g c path/to/component

Always generate the spec file.

Do NOT add extra test cases, helpers, or test setup until explicitly requested.

Leave the CLI spec stub as-is (should create only).

Services, facades, stores, and models stay handwritten.

After generating a component, only then edit template, styles, and class logic.

